                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b7a4c86a-c6c3-43d2-bf1b-1a9822d5996d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a1869b8-914c-3980-a5dc-9d27fcba701f",
                        "source_sense_id": "fbddaf8c-4318-3365-a6d7-a46b9cf5e2ac",
                        "target_lang_word": "materialise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "materialise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                        "entry_id": "0c59b9c2-f932-35b3-9419-54ca7566f5dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Non-Oxford British English standard spelling of materialize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "807e4d34-c032-4cb1-a130-e2dd9db9fa1c",
                                                "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                                "text": "Therefore, the new standard design in fact has materialised as a 4-6-2 with two 20 in. cylinders and a boiler pressure of 250 lb. per sq. in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29282658-495b-433b-8806-ee7efd806b5a",
                                                "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                                "text": "Third, while there is no immediate risk of Greece being kicked out of the club, such a threat could materialise if German taxpayers were to cut up rough and exert real political pressure on Angela Merkel's government."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de4e7da-56d6-4397-a895-9bda894e9604",
                                                "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                                "text": "In the old Irish folklore, this is a land where no one gets old or sick and where heroes live in comfort and tranquillity. But the land of Tír na nÓg only materialises to mere mortals at certain times, under certain circumstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9bcb0e3-78d8-46f9-b617-8da4cd6e7d35",
                                                "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                                "text": "J H Thomas, the union's general secretary, argued in a letter to union reps on September 23 [1919] that \"the long-made promise of a better world for railwaymen which was made at the time of the nation's crisis, and accepted by the railwaymen as an offer that would ultimately bear fruit, has not materialised\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59825aee-05f5-4c47-8a35-ac9eaec81ddd",
                                                "sense_id": "37c15b43-d707-3327-b246-8e31c25f98e6",
                                                "text": "Camara was the Paok equivalent of Bruno Fernandes: a playmaker adept at materialising in pockets and running his team."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e37e6b3-72a7-474c-97f0-e862a3746994",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a1869b8-914c-3980-a5dc-9d27fcba701f",
                        "source_sense_id": "fbddaf8c-4318-3365-a6d7-a46b9cf5e2ac",
                        "target_lang_word": "materialize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "materialize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b62c0e0-7037-3f80-a0fa-4722aeff9512",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe9ddd8-36bf-35e2-9f28-ef2d71de61b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to take physical form, or to cause an object to appear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "English",
                                            "Oxford",
                                            "US",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a59309d-e7e6-355e-8eaf-e951fa5f7357",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe9ddd8-36bf-35e2-9f28-ef2d71de61b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take physical form, to appear seemingly from nowhere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "English",
                                            "Oxford",
                                            "US",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "774aaf57-9215-49cd-b53b-133c151c9310",
                                                "sense_id": "4a59309d-e7e6-355e-8eaf-e951fa5f7357",
                                                "text": "a spirit form, temporarily materialized, and undistinguishable from a human being in the flesh, has come forth in the light[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5c35ab7-b9d3-4a12-b7ee-a6f73b77ce80",
                                                "sense_id": "4a59309d-e7e6-355e-8eaf-e951fa5f7357",
                                                "text": "Don’t you find, that things fail to materialize? Nothing materializes! Everything withers in the bud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ad6439a-c4fd-400e-8da8-0f712c8d4929",
                                                "sense_id": "4a59309d-e7e6-355e-8eaf-e951fa5f7357",
                                                "text": "Perhaps every five minutes each person ceases to exist and is fissed, with one descendant instantly replacing the original and the other materializing on a twin Earth somewhere […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b82ac00d-9320-4483-8249-9bcdb1542d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "4a59309d-e7e6-355e-8eaf-e951fa5f7357",
                                                "text": "And the citationality of these acts—and the calibration of such citationalities to each other—materializes as the very media forms in question."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cc8e00d-336e-339d-8e56-7cbb287d26d7",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe9ddd8-36bf-35e2-9f28-ef2d71de61b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become real (of a plan, idea, etc.); to come to fruition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "English",
                                            "Oxford",
                                            "US",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d6692fe-1800-3126-b110-64841ed1e353",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe9ddd8-36bf-35e2-9f28-ef2d71de61b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To regard as matter; to consider or explain by the laws or principles which are appropriate to matter."
                                        ],
